WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.700
Like the "Rocky" franchise before it, it's clear&nbsp;
that "Creed" can go the distance. With the third&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.660
installment hitting theaters soon, here's the&nbsp;
tale of the tape on this hard-hitting sequel.

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:14.100
The first two "Creed" films were both&nbsp;
released in November — November 25,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:20.640
2015 and November 21, 2018, to be exact — but&nbsp;
"Creed III" is bucking the trend. Originally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:27.000
it was supposed to hit theaters in November 2022,&nbsp;
but now, it has moved back to March 3, 2023.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:33.420
Why the change from late fall to late winter/early&nbsp;
spring? "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever" was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.220
released in November 2022, so it's a good bet&nbsp;
that United Artists and Warner Bros. didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:43.140
want to compete with that Marvel blockbuster.&nbsp;
And it's likely Ryan Coogler, the director of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.940
"Wakanda Forever" and an executive producer on&nbsp;
"Creed III," didn't want to compete with himself.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:53.640
So why not move it to November 2023? Most&nbsp;
likely because Warner Bros. is releasing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.900
another massive film that month — "Dune:&nbsp;
Part Two" — and chances are good the studio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:02.100
doesn't want two of its biggest films&nbsp;
duking it out for box office dominance.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.780
"Now we past talkin'."

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.632
"Then maybe you just have to fight him."

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.660
In the first "Creed" film, our titular&nbsp;
hero entered the world of prizefighting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:13.920
with a cancer-stricken Rocky Balboa as his&nbsp;
mentor. With the former champ by his side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.380
Adonis "Donnie" Creed grappled with his father's&nbsp;
complicated legacy and trained for a championship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:25.260
fight. The sequel saw Donnie and Rocky dealing&nbsp;
with the father-son pugilists Ivan and Viktor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:29.880
Drago. Ivan fought Rocky in "Rocky IV" after&nbsp;
killing Donnie's dad, Apollo Creed, in the ring.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:35.280
Despite coming to terms with his family history,&nbsp;
the past isn't done with Adonis Creed just yet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.900
In the third installment of the franchise, which&nbsp;
takes place seven years after the second film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:43.800
everything seems to be going right for&nbsp;
Donnie. He's the light heavyweight champion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:48.360
his musician wife Bianca is successful in&nbsp;
her own right, and everything is going great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:52.980
with their daughter, Amara. But that's&nbsp;
when Damian "Dame" Anderson shows up.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.140
Damian and Donnie were childhood friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.140 --> 00:02:00.300
but while the young Creed found success in the&nbsp;
ring, Damian wound up in prison for 18 years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:05.640
Now, he's out — and he's got some issues&nbsp;
with his former friend. A boxer himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:11.760
Damian feels robbed of his career, and he's here&nbsp;
to take everything Adonis has. Once like brothers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.057
these two rivals will have to settle&nbsp;
their differences inside the ring.

00:02:16.376 --> 00:02:20.468
The trailer for "Creed III" digs into&nbsp;
Donnie's relationship with Dame. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.468 --> 00:02:23.301
Donnie thanks the people in&nbsp;
his life for their success…

00:02:23.301 --> 00:02:31.380
"Bianca. Rocky. My dad. This&nbsp;
is built on their shoulders."

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:37.080
A quick flashback shows Donnie and Dame as young&nbsp;
boys, arms in the air, surrounded by cops. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:42.600
is likely the incident that sent Damian to prison&nbsp;
for 18 years. When his old friend is free, Donnie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:49.140
invites Dame back to the gym, and he's an absolute&nbsp;
monster in the ring. Naturally, animosity builds.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.080
"You think you mad? Try spending&nbsp;
half your life in a cell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:57.300
watching somebody else live your&nbsp;
life. I'm coming for everything."

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.180
The trailer ends with the two titans throwing down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.596
in the ring in the match touted&nbsp;
as the "Battle for Los Angeles."

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:10.260
"Creed III" features an absolutely stacked cast&nbsp;
of Hollywood A-listers. Michael B. Jordan reprises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:14.400
the role of Adonis "Donnie" Creed, and Tessa&nbsp;
Thompson also returns to play Bianca. Their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.960
daughter, Amara, is played by Mila Davis-Kent.&nbsp;
Other returning familiar faces include Phylicia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:24.120
Rashad as Donnie's mom, Mary Anne Creed,&nbsp;
and Wood Harris as Tony "Little Duke" Evers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:28.680
Creed's trainer. We'll also get to see the&nbsp;
return of Florian Munteanu as Viktor Drago.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:35.100
A new addition to the cast is Jonathan Majors as&nbsp;
Damian "Dame" Anderson. Majors has made quite a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:39.480
name for himself recently, starring in projects&nbsp;
like the horror series "Lovecraft Country" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:44.400
the Western "The Harder They Fall." Of course,&nbsp;
he also appeared as He Who Remains in "Loki" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:50.340
is set to be the MCU's next big bad as Kang the&nbsp;
Conqueror in "Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania."

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:55.500
Boxing fans should also keep an eye out for&nbsp;
cameos, too. Multiple-time champion Canelo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.760
Álvarez will be making his acting debut in the&nbsp;
film, and former cruiserweight champion Tony&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.663
Bellew will reprise his role as Ricky Conlan,&nbsp;
the antagonist of the first "Creed" film.

00:04:05.289 --> 00:04:09.720
Unfortunately, one major player who&nbsp;
won't be coming back in "Creed III"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:13.957
is Sylvester Stallone. In July&nbsp;
2022, he explained to Metro,

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.500
Saying the third film takes things in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:22.620
"different direction," Stallone&nbsp;
offered encouragement, saying,

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:30.120
But Stallone was a bit more critical in an&nbsp;
interview with the Hollywood Reporter, saying,

00:04:45.311 --> 00:04:50.580
After parts on TV shows including "The Wire," and&nbsp;
"Friday Night Lights," Michael B. Jordan finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:55.800
found A-list stardom by teaming up with director&nbsp;
Ryan Coogler and playing in a trio of powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:01.800
films — "Fruitvale Station," "Black Panther," and&nbsp;
"Creed." Now, after two decades in the business,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:06.720
Jordan is stepping behind the camera for&nbsp;
the first time to direct "Creed III."

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.280
"It's something I'm eternally grateful for."

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:11.201
According to Variety, Jordan&nbsp;
said in a press conference,

00:05:19.539 --> 00:05:23.100
Jordan has gotten wisdom from some&nbsp;
of the best. According to Empire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:28.140
he has learned about directing while acting from&nbsp;
Denzel Washington and Bradley Cooper. He also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:32.160
received guidance from Ryan Coogler.&nbsp;
Jordan shared that Coogler told him,

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:40.320
As for the screenplay, Jordan will&nbsp;
be working off a script written by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.220
Zach Baylin and Keenan Coogler, who also&nbsp;
worked with Ryan Coogler on the story.

